      "id": 1,
      "text": "Conroe was founded in 1881 by Union Cavalry officer Isaac Conroe as a lumber town, giving the city its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.iloveconroe.com/conroe-tx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A railroad stop called \"Conroe's Switch\" was named in the early days, later shortened to Conroe, and helped move lumber to market.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitconroe.com/plan/history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city flourished during the 1930s oil boom, adding a second wave of prosperity to its lumber roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.iloveconroe.com/conroe-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Downtown Conroe preserves its heritage with historic architecture, the Heritage Museum, and other local landmarks that echo its past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.iloveconroe.com/conroe-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Lone Star Monument and Historical Flag Park display flags that flew over Texas, each accompanied by a plaque explaining its significance.",
